# Bento Morph UI

All sections are one shared bento system. Never mount a separate page layout.

## Persistent boxes

- Eight boxes `A`–`H` live in `BentoGrid.jsx` as the same DOM nodes for every section.
- Section files (`HeroContent`, `AboutContent`, …) only export content for box IDs they use.
- `null` in `LAYOUTS` / `LAYOUTS_MOBILE` hides a box (opacity 0); do not unmount the box shell.
- Changing section = new grid placement + content fade. Framer `layout` morphs size/position.

## Transition contract

1. Outgoing content fades out.
2. Boxes reshape and reposition into the next section layout.
3. Unused boxes hide; needed boxes appear from the shared set (never brand-new page chrome).
4. Incoming content fades in after / with the morph.

## Motion

- Box morph: ease-in-out tween from `motion.js` (`BENTO_MORPH`) — not a slow spring.
- Content: short ease-in-out fade (`CONTENT_TRANSITION`).
- Keep in/out timing consistent; do not stack long staggered delays on section enter.

## Layout rules

- Desktop: 12×8 CSS grid. Placement: `[colStart, colEnd, rowStart, rowEnd]`.
- Prefer reusing the same box IDs across adjacent sections so the eye tracks the morph (e.g. Hero `B` → About `B` → Projects `B`).
- Do not replace the bento with cards-outside-grid, full-page scrolls, or per-section root layouts.
- Glass panel look stays on the box shell unless a layout entry explicitly overrides style (e.g. Projects filter row).

## Section content

- One job per box. Export named `A`–`H` functions only.
- Scroll inside a box with wheel/touch only (`.thin-scroll`). Never rely on ArrowUp/Down for card scroll.
